WEBVTT

00:06.530 --> 00:07.980
What's that?

00:13.620 --> 00:16.490
<i>That claw... He's from the Malebranche.</i>

00:16.490 --> 00:20.250
<i>But why? I'd better tell Mr. Maou fast.</i>

00:21.870 --> 00:23.440
You're all seeing this, right?

00:23.440 --> 00:24.620
Holy shit.

00:26.000 --> 00:30.380
<i>I can't feel anything... 
My idea link isn't getting through.</i>

00:30.380 --> 00:32.010
<i>I'll try Miss Suzuno.</i>

00:32.010 --> 00:34.800
Sasa-chii, what do you think that is?

00:34.800 --> 00:37.630
Huh? Um, I'm not sure!

00:37.630 --> 00:40.530
Maybe it's some kind of dangerous animal.

00:42.170 --> 00:44.520
<i>Demons everywhere, I'm sorry.</i>

01:07.830 --> 01:09.920
<b>The Devil is a Part-Timer! Season 2</b>

02:18.990 --> 02:23.950
m 370 218 l 609 218 609 245 370 245

02:19.570 --> 02:21.240
What's with this?

02:20.570 --> 02:23.950
<b>The Devil Gets Off to a Late Start</b>

02:20.570 --> 02:23.950
<b>The Devil Gets Off to a Late Start</b>

02:21.240 --> 02:23.950
Guess you can't trust 
the weather report, huh?

02:23.950 --> 02:25.510
Yo, Maou!

02:26.000 --> 02:28.290
Oh, how did the test go?

02:28.290 --> 02:29.610
I have little hope.

02:29.610 --> 02:32.250
We couldn't even read half the questions.

02:32.250 --> 02:36.880
Maybe you should hit pause on this test.
It seems like a waste of the application fee.

02:41.440 --> 02:44.010
Hey, what are you doing—

02:44.430 --> 02:46.520
Wh-Wh-What the heck was that?!

02:48.100 --> 02:51.010
Dad, I think he might be one.

02:51.520 --> 02:53.010
Can I take off my hat?

02:53.010 --> 02:54.650
Just don't attract attention.

03:00.990 --> 03:03.370
Is your hair—?!

03:03.370 --> 03:04.910
I was right!

03:05.610 --> 03:07.870
I guessed from your smell.

03:07.870 --> 03:09.660
My smell?

03:09.660 --> 03:13.080
Maou, you know Big Sis, don't you?

03:13.080 --> 03:14.630
"Big Sis"?

03:14.630 --> 03:17.380
My big sis, Alas Ramus.

03:18.510 --> 03:21.640
You mean she's your older sister?

03:21.640 --> 03:23.240
Yep! My big sis!

03:23.240 --> 03:26.670
So you're Alas Ramus's younger sister?

03:26.670 --> 03:28.280
Not her older one?

03:28.280 --> 03:29.020
Yep!

03:29.310 --> 03:35.510
What? But you're bigger than Alas Ramus,
 and you definitely look older...

03:35.510 --> 03:39.560
Sheesh, don't stare at me 
just 'cause I'm beautiful!

03:40.050 --> 03:41.530
I wanna punch her.

03:42.330 --> 03:45.450
This means you two are from Ente Isla, right?

03:46.280 --> 03:50.010
Now how about you tell me your real names?

03:52.290 --> 03:56.040
We have no proof you're not an enemy.

03:56.040 --> 04:00.590
Who are you, and how do you 
know we're from Ente Isla?

04:00.900 --> 04:03.350
That language sounds like Centrient.

04:03.350 --> 04:04.290
I'm—

04:04.290 --> 04:06.440
It's okay, Dad.

04:06.440 --> 04:10.060
Maou's not an angel. 
Even I can tell that much.

04:10.840 --> 04:15.810
My name is Acieth Alla! 
"Tsubasa" is my fake name!

04:16.370 --> 04:18.940
"Alla"... you picked 
"Tsubasa" based on meaning?

04:18.940 --> 04:22.010
Yep! "Tsubasa" sounds cool, right?

04:23.200 --> 04:27.030
So, I take it you and Acieth 
aren't blood relatives.

04:27.030 --> 04:29.240
And Sato is a fake name, right?

04:29.240 --> 04:35.460
I named myself Sato after a man 
I met when I came to Japan.

04:35.710 --> 04:39.010
I thought I knew 
of everyone here who'd come from

04:39.010 --> 04:41.550
or been associated with Ente Isla.

04:41.550 --> 04:46.220
I want to know who you are.
And you're also the first clue I've found.

04:46.550 --> 04:47.590
Clue?

04:49.200 --> 04:52.980
My friends and I are 
looking for Emilia Justina.

04:54.000 --> 04:56.400
She was in Japan until just recently,

04:57.050 --> 04:59.740
but we haven't seen her since she 
went to Ente Isla a few weeks ago.

04:59.740 --> 05:00.790
Emilia!

05:01.150 --> 05:02.740
You know Emilia?!

05:02.740 --> 05:05.490
Where is she? Where's Emilia?!

05:05.490 --> 05:08.740
Calm down! I told you, we can't contact her!

05:13.000 --> 05:15.300
Emilia went to...

05:15.300 --> 05:19.840
I figured you were probably 
connected to Emi. Guess I was right.

05:22.920 --> 05:26.010
Are you Emi's—I mean Emilia's...

05:26.990 --> 05:29.760
My name is Nord Justina.

05:29.760 --> 05:34.600
Emilia... is my precious daughter.

05:35.190 --> 05:37.020
<i>Pick up the phone, idiot!</i>

05:38.370 --> 05:39.520
An idea link?!

05:39.520 --> 05:41.770
Answer me at once!

05:41.770 --> 05:44.280
Suzuno? What's with the sudden link?

05:44.580 --> 05:46.930
It's your fault for not answering your phone.

05:46.930 --> 05:49.530
Get back to Sasazuka now. It's an emergency.

05:49.530 --> 05:54.210
Excuse me? Listen, I'm in 
the middle of something right now.

05:54.210 --> 05:56.060
<i>We have an SOS from Chiho!</i>

05:56.060 --> 05:57.040
What?!

05:57.040 --> 06:00.540
See the storm outside? 
It's centered around Sasazuka.

06:00.890 --> 06:03.100
Specifically, the good Chiho's school.

06:03.550 --> 06:05.200
What the hell?!

06:05.200 --> 06:07.550
<i>I don't know whether it's an 
angel, a demon, or a human,</i>

06:07.550 --> 06:10.420
but <i>someone</i> is deploying a massive spell.

06:10.420 --> 06:12.550
One that controls the weather.

06:12.550 --> 06:15.610
I don't know how long Lucifer 
and I can hold out alone.

06:15.610 --> 06:17.560
Get back here now!

06:18.050 --> 06:20.640
What the heck is going on?!

06:22.190 --> 06:24.490
What do I do with these two?

06:24.490 --> 06:25.940
Hey, Maou.

06:26.520 --> 06:28.720
I heard that lady's voice.

06:29.500 --> 06:31.450
You heard all that?

06:31.450 --> 06:34.660
Pretty much. What do you want to do?

06:34.660 --> 06:38.580
It's kind of bad for us if you disappear now.

06:38.580 --> 06:40.800
Right back at you.

06:40.800 --> 06:44.450
Ideally, I'd like to go back 
to Sasazuka with you right now.

06:44.450 --> 06:46.590
But how?

06:46.590 --> 06:48.330
Can the three of us fly there?

06:48.330 --> 06:50.780
I wouldn't be worried 
about this if we could!

06:50.780 --> 06:53.170
Just tell me what direction to go.

06:54.100 --> 06:55.350
Here!

06:59.370 --> 07:01.140
They're... floating?

07:02.600 --> 07:05.610
Acieth! You're drawing major 
attention to us right now!

07:08.220 --> 07:09.610
Which way, Maou?

07:09.610 --> 07:12.870
Crap, I'm all turned around now...

07:12.870 --> 07:16.730
The lady said there was a weather spell.

07:17.310 --> 07:19.250
So it must be that way!

07:19.250 --> 07:21.940
We gotta hurry, right? Let's zoom!

07:21.940 --> 07:22.970
W-Wait!

07:29.880 --> 07:31.410
W-Will we be okay?

07:31.410 --> 07:32.570
Maybe we should run.

07:32.570 --> 07:34.250
Teacher, what do we do?!

07:34.250 --> 07:35.170
I don't know!

07:35.170 --> 07:36.080
Teacher, let's go home!

07:36.080 --> 07:39.020
<i>There'll be a panic if I don't do something.</i>

07:40.210 --> 07:41.390
Huh? Hey!

07:41.390 --> 07:42.800
Sasa-chii?!

07:43.400 --> 07:46.710
<i>Mister Maou and the others 
might yell at me, but...</i>

07:52.650 --> 08:01.290
A new morning has come. 
It's a morning full of hope!

08:03.040 --> 08:08.050
Celestial force-using scum, 
are you the one who called me here?

08:08.050 --> 08:11.040
Thank goodness, you can speak Japanese.

08:11.040 --> 08:14.050
Who are you? Why did you summon me?

08:14.050 --> 08:17.530
There are a lot of reasons, 
but I wanted to speak to you

08:17.530 --> 08:22.810
before the teachers or the other students 
do something unwise to you.

08:23.150 --> 08:29.320
Hmph. You talk big for someone 
with so little celestial force.

08:30.100 --> 08:31.320
Um...

08:31.320 --> 08:34.570
Could you please use your 
power to open this door?

08:35.220 --> 08:37.460
You can do that if you're 
a Malebranche, right?

08:48.210 --> 08:51.790
You certainly look like 
a human from this country...

08:51.790 --> 08:55.620
Ah, you must be the one that 
brat Farfa was talking about.

08:55.620 --> 09:00.320
You're the new general, 
the MgRonald's barista?

09:00.320 --> 09:04.430
"Farfa"? Oh, Mister Farfarello.

09:05.330 --> 09:08.810
I guess I don't have to 
introduce myself, then.

09:10.660 --> 09:15.400
Best not to act if you're not an actor. 
I can hear your voice trembling.

09:15.400 --> 09:18.960
You can't hide fear from a demon.

09:19.830 --> 09:22.490
I am Libicocco.

09:22.490 --> 09:25.090
I am one of the Malebranche's leaders,

09:25.090 --> 09:28.330
but I'm not a namby-pamby baby like Farfa.

09:28.880 --> 09:32.840
I'm glad to know Demon King Satan is alive,

09:32.840 --> 09:36.340
but I will not acknowledge 
the new "great generals"!

09:41.220 --> 09:42.350
Mister Ashiya...

09:45.350 --> 09:48.290
Why are you sitting there silently?

09:48.290 --> 09:50.480
Well, um...

09:50.480 --> 09:52.920
I told you to explain this.

09:52.920 --> 09:57.370
Yes, ma'am, I understand 
what you're saying, but...

09:57.370 --> 10:00.890
I've always thought there was 
a lot of mystery about you,

10:00.890 --> 10:06.370
but I figured we weren't c-c-close enough 
for me to ask personal questions yet.

10:06.370 --> 10:07.920
I see...

10:07.920 --> 10:10.820
But this just doesn't make sense.

10:10.820 --> 10:12.390
I imagine not.

10:12.390 --> 10:16.880
I'll ask you again: Where did
 Suzuno and Urushihara go?

10:16.880 --> 10:20.290
In this rain! <i>Through the window</i>!

10:21.210 --> 10:22.550
Th-The truth is...

10:22.550 --> 10:23.410
Yes?

10:23.410 --> 10:26.570
K-Kamazuki and Urushihara are...

10:26.570 --> 10:27.390
Mm-hmm?

10:27.390 --> 10:32.240
They're, um, testing this health drink...

10:32.240 --> 10:32.980
And?

10:32.980 --> 10:35.650
And you could call that an effect of it...

10:35.650 --> 10:38.400
The slogan's, "Gets you going," 
not, "Gets you flying"!

10:38.720 --> 10:42.660
And the house across from here 
has to be over ten meters away!

10:42.660 --> 10:45.490
No way could they jump there, 
especially not without a running start!

10:45.490 --> 10:47.620
If they <i>can</i>, they better win Japan the gold!

10:47.620 --> 10:48.910
You're quite right.

10:48.910 --> 10:53.200
Plus, you seemed disapproving 
rather than surprised.

10:53.200 --> 10:56.170
It clearly wasn't the first time 
you've seen something like that!

10:56.820 --> 11:01.800
Miss Suzuki, I'm not sure you'd 
believe the truth if I told you.

11:03.010 --> 11:07.150
I'm not such a fool that I can't 
believe what I see with my own eyes.

11:07.610 --> 11:08.310
Understood.

11:10.080 --> 11:14.060
Miss Suzuki, we're not actually from Japa—

11:15.320 --> 11:18.300
Open up, Ashiya!

11:18.820 --> 11:22.800
Open the window, Ashiya!

11:22.800 --> 11:26.080
Sire! Why are you entering 
through the window?!

11:27.520 --> 11:29.580
Who are these people?!

11:31.330 --> 11:34.330
So cold... I'll explain later.

11:34.330 --> 11:36.580
Gonna leave him here for now.

11:36.580 --> 11:38.220
M-Mister Maou?

11:38.220 --> 11:40.890
Oh, you're here, Rika Suzuki?

11:42.580 --> 11:45.570
Well, I'm in a hurry, so we'll talk later.

11:46.100 --> 11:48.350
Ashiya, you're in charge of him.

11:48.870 --> 11:52.230
We can't afford to let him 
out of our sight right now.

11:52.230 --> 11:55.320
Sire, I don't understand what's—

11:55.320 --> 11:57.150
Maou, can we go?

11:57.150 --> 11:58.560
Yeah, thanks.

11:59.060 --> 12:00.860
Sorry, Ashiya. We'll talk later.

12:00.860 --> 12:03.610
Sire, is that girl—

12:03.610 --> 12:05.580
Okay, here we go!

12:05.580 --> 12:07.870
Sorry! Talk later!

12:11.210 --> 12:13.930
M-May I have some dry clothes?

12:13.930 --> 12:15.730
Who the hell are you?!

12:15.730 --> 12:19.480
He just <i>flew</i>!

12:27.430 --> 12:29.010
So who's this?

12:30.810 --> 12:32.390
<b>Go, Sasahata crowd!</b>

12:31.930 --> 12:33.310
I don't know.

12:34.810 --> 12:39.040
I'm sorry, Miss Suzuki. I'm about to be rude.

12:39.040 --> 12:40.150
Huh?

12:40.150 --> 12:41.820
Do you speak this language?

12:41.820 --> 12:45.320
You're not from Japan either?

12:47.700 --> 12:52.080
Neither was Maou. Who are you two?

12:52.080 --> 12:56.080
Frankly, I'd like to ask you that. 
Who are you?

12:56.080 --> 13:00.920
I used to be a farmer in Saint Aire.

13:00.920 --> 13:08.090
I assumed I'd die without ever 
setting foot outside my hometown.

13:08.090 --> 13:13.980
Then I assumed responsibility for 
protecting Tsubasa, and I crossed worlds...

13:13.980 --> 13:17.350
in order to deliver her to a certain someone.

13:17.350 --> 13:21.900
"Deliver" her? Is Tsubasa 
the girl that Maou was with?

13:21.900 --> 13:22.780
Yes.

13:22.780 --> 13:26.860
I take it she's an incarnation of Yesod?

13:26.860 --> 13:31.870
Are you... Are you Emilia Justina's father?

13:31.870 --> 13:33.370
"Emilia"?

13:33.370 --> 13:38.630
You're... Ah, I see. I can hardly believe it.

13:39.240 --> 13:41.090
You two must be...

13:41.090 --> 13:45.660
No, Mister Maou must be the 
"chosen one" my wife spoke of.

13:45.660 --> 13:46.890
Chosen one?

13:46.890 --> 13:47.680
Hey.

13:47.680 --> 13:49.050
Something my wife said.

13:49.050 --> 13:49.980
Hello?

13:50.850 --> 13:55.270
"When a chosen one is prepared 
to expose the truth of the world,

13:55.270 --> 13:56.820
bring the wings to our daughter."

13:57.970 --> 14:02.400
When Mister Maou said my 
daughter's name, I began to suspect.

14:02.400 --> 14:04.030
What does that—

14:04.030 --> 14:04.980
Listen to me!

14:05.540 --> 14:08.210
I don't know what secret 
understanding you have here,

14:08.210 --> 14:10.500
but let me in on it!

14:10.500 --> 14:12.850
Y-You're scary, miss.

14:12.850 --> 14:18.680
You better learn to watch your tongue 
if you wanna make it in Japan, Pops.

14:18.680 --> 14:19.670
"Pops"...?

14:19.670 --> 14:25.300
I'll tell you, I promise. 
So please, sit down.

14:25.300 --> 14:28.320
I-I won't be distracted so easily!

14:28.320 --> 14:29.680
What?

14:29.680 --> 14:31.820
So? What's the deal?

14:31.820 --> 14:33.100
This man...

14:33.100 --> 14:34.370
Right.

14:34.370 --> 14:36.180
...says he's Yusa's father.

14:36.180 --> 14:37.170
Right.

14:38.390 --> 14:39.200
Huh?

14:39.950 --> 14:44.570
What brings you to Japan, 
Mister Ribikok? Or, well, to Earth.

14:45.370 --> 14:48.130
Your pronunciation pisses me off.

14:48.800 --> 14:51.320
It's Libicocco! Say it.

14:51.320 --> 14:53.160
L-Libikoko...

14:53.160 --> 14:53.990
I'll kill you!

14:53.990 --> 14:55.080
What?!

14:55.080 --> 15:01.280
Know this: If a human messed up 
Draghignazzo's or Scarmiglione's name,

15:01.280 --> 15:04.090
they'd be headless in no time.

15:04.090 --> 15:08.590
Dra... D-Draggi-wh-what?!

15:08.590 --> 15:10.820
Again. Libicocco.

15:11.190 --> 15:12.350
Libicocco!

15:12.350 --> 15:13.650
Libicocco!

15:13.650 --> 15:14.950
Libicocco!

15:14.950 --> 15:17.390
There! You're not bad when you try.

15:17.390 --> 15:19.100
Th-Thanks.

15:19.100 --> 15:23.610
So, Mister Ri—Libicocco, 
what brings you to Japan?

15:24.290 --> 15:25.610
I came to rampage.

15:25.610 --> 15:26.730
Huh?

15:34.740 --> 15:36.490
Please stop!

15:55.410 --> 15:57.390
N-No...

15:59.860 --> 16:02.740
Is it me, or is the storm getting stronger?

16:02.740 --> 16:04.840
Yep! Wanna hurry more?

16:04.840 --> 16:08.400
No, I'm telling you, slow <i>down</i>!

16:12.150 --> 16:16.270
Please stop! Why are you doing this?

16:16.270 --> 16:17.160
Hmm?

16:17.450 --> 16:22.660
I was just told to go on a conspicuous 
rampage where the Gate dumped me.

16:23.210 --> 16:24.670
"Conspicuous"?

16:25.730 --> 16:31.670
Right now you, the kids inside, 
and everyone in the neighborhood

16:31.670 --> 16:34.370
are scared, right?

16:35.680 --> 16:39.060
This is a delectable mission for a demon.

16:39.670 --> 16:45.190
I can drink in mass fear, sorrow, and magic!

16:52.140 --> 16:56.070
Can't breathe... It's too much magic.

16:57.330 --> 16:59.080
You're pathetic.

17:03.530 --> 17:07.320
If you don't like what I'm doing, 
Miss MgRonald's Barista General,

17:07.320 --> 17:10.820
then force me to stop.

17:10.820 --> 17:13.590
I'll take you up on that.

17:17.590 --> 17:21.100
I'm technically one of 
the new generals, after all.

17:21.100 --> 17:23.490
I'll stop you by force.

17:23.490 --> 17:24.570
Miss Suzuno!

17:24.570 --> 17:26.270
I'm sorry I'm late.

17:26.960 --> 17:30.740
The storm wall suddenly got stronger, 
and it took some time to break through.

17:30.740 --> 17:31.660
Hey!

17:31.980 --> 17:36.990
You say that like you did it on your own.

17:36.990 --> 17:39.240
Mr. Urushihara, are those...?

17:39.240 --> 17:41.240
Hmm? Oh, these?

17:41.240 --> 17:43.140
I gave him some Holyvitan.

17:43.810 --> 17:45.790
That's why his wings are white?

17:45.790 --> 17:49.810
Sheesh, if I'd known he was 
gonna rampage this much,

17:49.810 --> 17:51.440
I would've inhaled some magic.

17:51.440 --> 17:53.740
Lucifer, if that's a joke, it's not funny!

17:53.740 --> 17:57.760
Lucifer and... You must be Deathscythe Bel.

17:59.260 --> 18:01.430
You know of me?

18:01.430 --> 18:02.520
Yes.

18:02.520 --> 18:06.520
I'll admit I didn't know you were here...

18:07.780 --> 18:10.330
but it's very convenient.

18:11.520 --> 18:16.030
Miss Rika, thank you 
for your goodness to Emilia.

18:16.030 --> 18:18.500
M-My pleasure.

18:18.500 --> 18:20.780
U-Um, Mister Ashiya?

18:20.780 --> 18:21.610
Yes?

18:21.610 --> 18:23.350
Who is Emilia?

18:23.350 --> 18:28.330
Emi Yusa. Her real name is Emilia Justina.

18:28.330 --> 18:30.450
Emi isn't Japanese?!

18:30.450 --> 18:31.510
Correct.

18:35.670 --> 18:40.680
Yusa—or rather, Emilia—isn't 
from anywhere on Earth.

18:41.710 --> 18:43.180
What does that mean?

18:43.590 --> 18:49.190
This is an oversimplification, 
but you can think of Yusa as an alien.

18:50.120 --> 18:55.690
She came from somewhere far from Earth. 
She's human, but of another world.

18:57.220 --> 18:58.700
Do you think I'm stupid?

18:59.340 --> 19:01.980
If you can't believe me about this,

19:01.980 --> 19:07.700
I'm afraid I can't explain what you've seen.

19:07.700 --> 19:09.870
What I've seen?

19:10.710 --> 19:14.870
The house across from here 
has to be over ten meters away.

19:15.370 --> 19:19.220
Could any Earthling jump to it, 
and without a running start?

19:20.610 --> 19:24.470
No way. You're kidding. 
Are you messing with me?

19:24.470 --> 19:28.470
I imagine I'd say the same thing 
in your place.

19:28.470 --> 19:30.290
Show me proof!

19:30.680 --> 19:36.230
It doesn't make sense for an alien to be 
working part-time and living on the cheap!

19:36.230 --> 19:38.450
I can't argue with that.

19:38.450 --> 19:43.490
Still, even aliens have to 
work in order to eat.

19:43.990 --> 19:47.740
It's only natural she doesn't believe us.

19:47.740 --> 19:51.250
If someone told me about a country 
as technologically advanced as this,

19:51.250 --> 19:56.000
I'd dismiss it as ridiculous.

19:56.000 --> 19:59.460
Did Maou tell you who we are?

19:59.460 --> 20:04.510
No, but I'm fairly sure you're not human.

20:04.510 --> 20:05.530
However...

20:06.780 --> 20:09.770
It looks as if we'll have to 
postpone your introduction.

20:18.780 --> 20:20.690
They have us surrounded.

20:21.080 --> 20:24.650
I've never seen that armor. 
Do you recognize it?

20:24.650 --> 20:26.030
From the Eastern Continent...

20:26.450 --> 20:29.360
The second-highest ranking 
of Efzahan's knight squadrons:

20:29.360 --> 20:31.480
the Inlaid Azure Scarves.

20:32.540 --> 20:35.040
What are they doing here?

20:35.040 --> 20:37.780
Wh-What are you two talking about?

20:37.780 --> 20:41.420
Miss Rika isn't part of this. 
We need to protect her. Right?

20:41.990 --> 20:43.000
Yes.

20:44.930 --> 20:46.810
Can you fight?

20:46.810 --> 20:52.280
At home, I'd have no trouble against 
an army this size, but here...

20:52.280 --> 20:57.190
I'm not much better. 
I've never been formally trained.

20:57.190 --> 20:59.190
Are they after me?

20:59.190 --> 21:03.910
No—if I hadn't met Mister Maou, 
I wouldn't be here.

21:04.630 --> 21:06.220
One of you, then?

21:06.220 --> 21:07.890
Presumably, yes.

21:10.040 --> 21:14.670
If we assume the disturbance at 
Miss Sasaki's school is a diversion,

21:15.200 --> 21:19.840
their aim is whoever has the highest 
chance of staying here in a crisis.

21:19.840 --> 21:25.910
Only one of us currently 
lacks the power to fight...

21:28.720 --> 21:31.780
The enemy was after me all along?

21:39.230 --> 21:43.420
Ugh, what rain! Should I hail a cab?

21:43.420 --> 21:48.680
Maybe it's not worth it, since 
I'm not going far from the station...

21:51.260 --> 21:52.490
What's this?

21:54.520 --> 21:57.330
Well, no cab for me.

21:57.330 --> 22:00.730
Damn it, there's no bath in that building!

22:02.450 --> 22:03.450
Okay!
